{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L138-L161","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript), §3b-conditional on\n`QouObstructionReductionContext`:\n\n**Theorem.** Let `(𝐂, A, τ)` be a quantum observable universe.  Then\n(a) the classical-limit obstruction is one-dimensional\n`dim HH²(U_q,Ad) = 1`; (b) its unique class is the trace image of the\nEuler characteristic; (c) the level-`n` obstruction vanishes iff\n`n ∣ χ(A)`.\n\nPart (a) is **derived** from the two inputs (Van den Bergh CY-3 duality\ncomposed with Drinfeld rigidity).  Parts (b),(c) reduce to the single\nhonest trace gap `obstruction_trace_gap`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:qou-obstruction-reduction","label":"thm:qou-obstruction-reduction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/qou-obstruction-reduction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_vanishes_iff_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_vanishes_iff_chi","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L125-L136","doc":"**Derived (conclusion (c)).**  Kummer level-`n` vanishing ⟺ `n ∣ χ(A)`.\nComposes the *definitional* `kappa_vanishes_def` (over `κ₀`) with the\nresidual identification `κ₀ = χ(A)` (`obstruction_trace_gap`).  Both are\nsorry-free; the derivation is §3b-conditional on\n`QouObstructionReductionContext`, whose fields (`hattori_stallings`,\n`trace_pairing_cast`, `chern_character`) carry the domain gap as explicit\n*hypotheses* rather than as a `sorry`.  This is **not** a class field —\nthe χ(A)-form of vanishing is *derived*, never assumed (that assumption\nwas the self-projection this file removed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_trace_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_trace_gap","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L107-L123","doc":"**Residual cohomology gap.**  The Euler/trace pairing on the\ngenerator of the one-dimensional `HH²(U_q, Ad)` evaluates to `χ(A)`,\nso `κ₀ = χ(A)` and the trace image is `χ(A)`.  This is the explicit\nConnes / Hattori–Stallings pairing computation — the disjoint tensor\ndecomposition of the adjoint bimodule together with the commutation\nof the Markov trace with the coproduct — which is NOT derivable from\nthe two structural inputs (`vdb_duality`, `drinfeld_rigidity`) and is\nleft as the honest domain gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.obstruction_class_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.obstruction_class_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L100-L105","doc":"The obstruction class **is** `χ(A)`, definitionally. This is the equation\nthe downstream evaluations rewrite along, so that each is visibly an\nevaluation of the one class rather than of a private copy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.obstruction_class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.obstruction_class","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L87-L98","doc":"**The universal obstruction class `χ(A) ∈ HH²(U_q, Ad) ≅ ℤ`**, under the\nname its consumers use.\n\nA pure accessor for the existing `chi_A` field — it introduces no new datum\nand no new hypothesis. `SkeinResolutionObstruction` is documented as being\n\"cross-wired to the **same** `QouObstructionReductionContext` … via\n`obstruction_class_eq`\", i.e. deliberately reading the one canonical class\nrather than carrying a free field of its own; that wiring just had no name\non this side. Adding it here keeps the single-source-of-truth property the\nde-axiomatisation (bean `7kzn`) was for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.chern_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.chern_character","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Chern character map property identifying the trace image of the HH² generator with χ(A) via trace pairing ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.trace_pairing_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.trace_pairing_cast","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The trace pairing on Z acts as casting to Reals ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hattori_stallings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hattori_stallings","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Hattori-Stallings trace property relating the primitive Kummer obstruction κ₀ to the Euler characteristic χ(A) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.trace_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.trace_pairing","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Structural trace evaluation map from algebraic K-theory K₀(A) to Hochschild homology HH₀(A) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa_vanishes_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa_vanishes_def","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L77-L77","doc":"DEFINITIONAL — Kummer level-`n` vanishing *is* `n ∣ κ₀`\n(definition of the predicate, in terms of `κ₀`, NOT `χ(A)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa_vanishes","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Kummer level-`n` vanishing predicate `κ₀ ≡ 0 (mod n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.kappa0","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The primitive Kummer obstruction integer `κ₀` (distinct datum;\nits equality with `χ(A)` is the residual gap, not assumed here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.phi_1_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.phi_1_image","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Trace image of the `HH²` generator (observation-frame value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.chi_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.chi_A","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Euler characteristic `χ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.drinfeld_rigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.drinfeld_rigidity","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L65-L65","doc":"INPUT — **Drinfeld rigidity** of the quasi-triangular deformation:\nthe degree-1 Hochschild homology (the deformation module) is\none-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.vdb_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.vdb_duality","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L61-L61","doc":"INPUT — **Van den Bergh / Calabi–Yau duality of dimension 3** for\n`U_q(su₂)`: `HH^i(U_q,Ad) ≅ HH_{3-i}(U_q,Ad)`, hence equal\ndimension.  (A literature theorem; the class instance is the\n§3b-cond conditional hypothesis.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hhHomDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hhHomDim","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L56-L56","doc":"`dim_k HH_i(U_q, Ad)`, the Hochschild homology dimensions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hhCohDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.hhCohDim","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L54-L54","doc":"`dim_k HH^i(U_q, Ad)`, the Hochschild cohomology dimensions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QouObstructionReductionContext","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean#L47-L85","doc":"**§3b-cond context** for `thm:qou-obstruction-reduction`.\n\nFields are the genuine *hypotheses / data* of the reduction — the\ndownstream conclusion `dim HH² = 1` is derived from them, never carried\nas a field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}